 "answer": "Maize is grown most in Iowa, covering 4,601,295 hectares (54.56% of the harvested area), followed by soybean on 3,786,696 hectares (44.9% of the area) [S1]. These two crops make up the vast majority of the harvested area in the state according to MapSPAM 2020 estimates [S1]. Other crops grown include minor amounts of other cereals, wheat, and vegetables [S1].\n\nWould you like to know about the rotation practices commonly used with these crops in the region?",
